+/// EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED (default on; =0 restores the old behaviour): a GPU-written render
+/// target whose relocation shape is guarded still dies once it has been untouched for
+/// SupersededFrames and a render target of a different shape, touched since, covers its memory --
+/// the game reused that memory for another layout, so the old contents have no reader left.
+/// Ported from Fritchii v5.6 (EXP58, f549632a), measured at Castle Town over 150 s: device memory
+/// 7.8-10.5 -> 5.2-5.7 GB, collector evictions 83-1915 a window -> 0, worst frames 140-180 ->
+/// 30-48 ms. Never applied to a shape the CPU read.
+inline bool SupersededSweepEnabled() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED");
+        return value == nullptr || value[0] != '0';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
